# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with an idle keepalive.
#
# The harness runs the image CMD so services actually boot. The CMD is
# PID-1-safe:
#   * sshd + WinRM are started first;
#   * all three ManageEngine services (Apache, Notification Server and
#     DesktopCentralServer) are started via Start-Service, so none of them is
#     PID 1;
#   * PID 1 is an idle `while ($true) { Start-Sleep 60 }` loop.
#
# Desktop Central's licence agreement is answered once at BUILD time (see the
# Dockerfile and dc-register.bat), so DesktopCentralServer is an ordinary
# Windows service here: Start-Service brings it up and Stop-Service takes it
# down. There is no detached console-mode wrapper to hunt for.
#
# Consequence for solutions: ManageEngine Desktop Central is ALREADY RUNNING
# with the vulnerable config, so a fix must restart or stop the affected
# component (safe now - it is not PID 1) for the live checks to pass.
# Restarting or stopping a service can never kill the container.
